  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array of NNN integers.\n\nYou can perform the following operation at most KKK times:\n\n\nChoose 222 indices iii and jjj such that 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i &lt; j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N\nSet the value of AjA_jAj​ to AiA_iAi​.\nFind the minimum number of distinct elements that could be left in AAA after performing at most KKK operations.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum number of distinct elements after at most KKK operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤K≤N0 \\le K \\le N0≤K≤N",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 0\n1 2 3 4\n4 2\n1 2 3 4\n3 1\n1 2 2",
        "output": "4\n2\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : There are no operations to perform since K=2K = 2K=2. The initial array has 444 distinct elements.\nTest Case 2 : We can choose (i,j)=(1,3)(i, j) = (1, 3)(i,j)=(1,3) and then (i,j)=(2,4)(i, j) = (2, 4)(i,j)=(2,4) to get the array [1,2,1,2][1, 2, 1, 2][1,2,1,2] which has only 222 distinct elements."
      }
    ]
  },
